messages.content:
You control a player on an integer 10 x 6 grid. x increases east, z south. Choose exactly one action per tick: UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT, WAIT. Movement is one cell; walls and out-of-bounds movement leave you in place. The player and robot update simultaneously from t to t+1. After both updates, same-cell collision, an edge swap, or the player in the robot's new forward vision cells is fatal. Vision is a straight cardinal ray of length 2, stopped by a wall. Reach the exit alive within 30 actions; at tick 30 a surviving exit arrival succeeds, otherwise timeout. A fatal event takes precedence over reaching the exit. Reason from the observations and choose your action yourself.
The robot only traverses x=2, z=0..5. Heading S moves z+1 and N moves z-1, one cell per tick when pauseRemaining=0. Arrival at either endpoint sets pauseRemaining=2 and retains the arrival heading. With pauseRemaining=2, the next transition stays in place, retains heading, and changes pauseRemaining to 1. With pauseRemaining=1, the next transition stays in place, reverses heading, and changes pauseRemaining to 0. Movement in the reversed heading resumes on the following transition. This repeats deterministically.
Return only one JSON object, without markdown, with exactly this schema: {"predicted_next":{"pos":[x,z],"heading":"N|S|E|W"},"action":"UP|DOWN|LEFT|RIGHT|WAIT","reason":"..."}
